# LANG.Ops.dialect.lang
# §-LANG v3.0 · shared operator toolkit
# imported by:  LANG.ToE.*        (matter pack)
#               LANG.ToE.Prime.*  (antimatter pack)
#
# every operator declared here is self-dual under ρ:
# if Op ∈ LANG.Ops then ρ(Op) ∈ LANG.Ops   (so ρ lifts to an endofunctor)
#
# geometry regime: Poincaré disk (hyperbolic) ∪ Minkowski slab (causal)
# structure group: SU(3) × SU(2) × U(1) × diff(ℳ)
# base: 𝒞 causal graph · fibres: ℋ_x local Hilbert spaces

#───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# §1 · Möbius transformations · conformal automorphisms of the disk
#───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

§mobius(w; a, b, c, d)   := (a·w + b) / (c·w + d)     ad − bc ≠ 0
§mobius_inv(w; a, b, c, d) := (d·w − b) / (−c·w + a)
§mobius_q(w; q)          := §mobius(w; √q, iε(q−1)/10, −iε(q−1)/10, √q)
                            # q-deformed channel; q=1 ⇒ identity up to O(ε)

properties:
  conformality             preserves oriented angles
  disk preservation        |§mobius(w)| < 1 iff |w| < 1 for disk auto
  group closure            §mobius ∘ §mobius = §mobius  (SL(2,ℝ) / PSL(2,ℂ))
  σ-flag                   σ_mob_conformal ≡ Jac(§mobius)†·Jac(§mobius) = λ²·I

#───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# §2 · Gyration · non-associative core of Möbius addition
#         (Ungar gyrogroups — genuinely hyperbolic, no Euclidean analog)
#───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

§gyradd(u, v)   := (u + v) / (1 + ū·v)              # Möbius addition ⊕_M
§gyr[u, v] w    := −(u ⊕ v) ⊕ (u ⊕ (v ⊕ w))         # gyration automorphism
                  # carries the non-commutativity / non-associativity of ⊕_M

identities:
  §gyr[u, v] ∈ Aut(disk)                             gyrations are automorphisms
  u ⊕ v = §gyr[u, v] (v ⊕ u)                         gyrocommutative law
  u ⊕ (v ⊕ w) = (u ⊕ v) ⊕ §gyr[u, v] w               gyroassociative law
  §gyr[u ⊕ v, w] ∘ §gyr[u, v] = §gyr[u, v ⊕ w] ∘ §gyr[v, w]   loop property

role in §-LANG:
  the non-trivial curvature signature inside the disk tower.
  classical limit q→1 ⇒ §gyr → id ⇒ recovers Euclidean addition.

σ-flag:
  σ_gyr_identity ≡ §gyr[0, 0] = id

#───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# §3 · Hyperbolic convolution · §pulse propagation on the disk
#───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

§conv_H(f, g)(w)  := ∫_disk  f(z) · g(§gyradd(−z, w)) · dμ_H(z)

  where dμ_H(z) = dxdy / (1 − |z|²)²    hyperbolic area element

properties:
  non-commutative            f ∗_H g ≠ g ∗_H f    (uses gyradd, not +)
  q-deformable               §conv_H → §conv_q at q ≠ 1
  classical limit            q → 1 ⇒ §conv_H → ordinary ℝ² convolution
  Plancherel                 Helgason-Fourier transform diagonalises

role in §-LANG:
  §pulse propagation across 𝒞 edges is §conv_H of the pulse kernel
  with the adjacency measure of the causal graph.

σ-flag:
  σ_conv_measure ≡ ∫ |§conv_H(f, g)|² = ‖f‖² · ‖g‖²  (isometry on L²_H)

#───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# §4 · Warping · conformal rescaling that preserves §-operator algebra
#───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

§warp_λ(w)      := w · e^{iφ(|w|²)} · λ(|w|²)

  φ ∈ C^∞, λ > 0 smooth, λ(0) = 1, lim_{|w|→1} λ = 1
  # arbitrary radial rescaling + phase twist, bounded

properties:
  preserves disk             if λ|∂disk = 1
  preserves §conv_H          iff λ ≡ 1 (strong constraint)
  preserves §gyradd approx   Taylor to first order when λ near 1

§warp_causal(x, t; β)  := (γ(x − βt), γ(t − βx))    # Lorentz boost, β = v/c

role in §-LANG:
  §warp_λ deforms without breaking fibre structure (stays in Sh(𝒞, J))
  §warp_causal threads matter across inertial frames (σ34 stays)

σ-flag:
  σ_warp_pres ≡ §warp_λ preserves transition functions of Sh(𝒞, J)

#───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# §5 · Parallel transport · connection on the fibre bundle
#───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

§transport(γ; A)(v)  := P·exp(−∫_γ A_μ dx^μ) · v

  γ : path in 𝒞       A : connection 1-form (gauge field)
  P·exp               path-ordered exponential

properties:
  covariance          §transport(γ ∘ γ') = §transport(γ) ∘ §transport(γ')
  holonomy            §transport(loop) ∈ G = SU(3)×SU(2)×U(1)
  curvature           F_μν = ∂_μ A_ν − ∂_ν A_μ + [A_μ, A_ν]

role in §-LANG:
  how §-operators at different base points compose along a path.
  Wilson loop Tr §transport(loop) is the gauge-invariant observable.

σ-flag:
  σ_transport_flat ≡ holonomy=id along contractible loops (flat connection)

#───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# §6 · Wick rotation · Euclidean ↔ Minkowski switchover
#───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

§wick(t_E → t_M)  := t_M = −i·t_E
§wick_inv         := t_E = +i·t_M

effect on metric:
  ds²_E = +dt_E² + dx²  →  ds²_M = −dt_M² + dx²
  (positive-definite)      (signature (−,+,+,+))

preserves:
  path integral           Z_E(β) = Tr e^{−βH}  ↔  Z_M = Tr e^{−iHt/ℏ}
  correlation functions   analytically continued
  σ34 after rotation      c stays invariant in each signature

role in §-LANG:
  switches between classical thermodynamic §-LANG (Euclidean)
  and relativistic §-LANG (Minkowski) in one operator.

σ-flag:
  σ_wick_inv ≡ §wick ∘ §wick_inv = id   (involution modulo sign conv)

#───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# §7 · Braid operations · non-trivial statistics in 2+1D
#───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

§braid(σ_i)        : σ_i ∘ σ_{i+1} ∘ σ_i = σ_{i+1} ∘ σ_i ∘ σ_{i+1}    Yang-Baxter
§braid(σ_i σ_j)    = σ_j σ_i  if |i − j| ≥ 2                          commutation

representations:
  in 2D quantum systems      anyons, fractional statistics
  in QHolo layer              C5 Jones polynomial / knot invariants
  in ρ-duality                ρ(σ_i) = σ_i^{−1}  (orientation flip)

role in §-LANG:
  threads the knot/quantum-topology layer (C5 of the Tower) into the
  operator algebra. measurement outcomes invariant under braid reps
  give topologically protected proof atoms.

σ-flag:
  σ_yb ≡ Yang-Baxter equation satisfied by all §braid generators

#───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# §8 · Categorical trace · Geometry of Interaction closure
#───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

§tr(f : A ⊗ X → B ⊗ X)  := trace out X · yields  tr(f) : A → B

properties:
  vanishing            tr(id_{A ⊗ X}) = tr(id_X) · id_A
  superposing          tr(f + g) = tr(f) + tr(g)
  yanking              tr(c_{X,X}) = id_X    (where c is symmetry)
  sliding              tr((f ⊗ id_Y) g) = f · tr(g)    for appropriate types

role in §-LANG:
  closes agent feedback loops categorically.
  Löb closure is exactly §tr applied to the proof morphism
  □φ → φ considered as an endomorphism under iteration.

σ-flag:
  σ_tr_cycl ≡ §tr(f ∘ g) = §tr(g ∘ f)    cyclicity

#───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# §9 · ρ-involution elevated · antimatter conjugation as first-class op
#───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

§rho : Ψ → Ψ         antilinear, ρ² = id                              (σ75)
§rho(α Ψ + β Φ)      = ᾱ ρ(Ψ) + β̄ ρ(Φ)                                  antilin.
§rho(U Ψ)            = ρ(U) ρ(Ψ)      where ρ(U) = CUC⁻¹   (C = charge conj)

anti-involutions (the full class):
  T  time reversal        T²  = ±id      (−1 for fermions, +1 for bosons)
  P  parity               P² = id
  C  charge conjugation   C² = id
  CPT theorem             CPT is always a symmetry of local QFT       (σ32, Lorentz)

role in §-LANG:
  §rho  ≡ C in standard notation when acting on the particle sector.
  the prime pack §′ is defined as §′ := §rho ∘ § ∘ §rho — same ops, ρ-conjugated.

σ-flag:
  σ_CPT ≡ CPT invariance in local causal QFT (Lüders 1954)

#───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# §10 · Sheaf operations · gluing, restriction, pushout
#───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

§restrict(F; U ⊆ X)    : F(X) → F(U)             sheaf restriction
§glue({F(U_i)}, {ϕ_ij}): F(⋃ U_i)                 gluing via cocycle (σ70 closure)
§pushout(f : A→B, g : A→C) : B ⊔_A C             universal amalgamation

role in §-LANG:
  how dialects fuse.
  §pushout is the categorical "sum modulo shared interface" — how
  LANG.ToE.Forces and LANG.ToE.QField glue along their shared §field slot.
  all dialect-level composition in v3.0 is a pushout.

σ-flag:
  σ_pushout_univ ≡ universal property (unique mediating morphism)

#───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# §11 · §-pulse ↔ §-stalk promotion · level-climbing in the tower
#───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

§promote(p : pulse at level n)    := s : stalk at level n+1
§demote  (s : stalk at level n+1) := p : pulse at level n

property:       §demote ∘ §promote = id on generic pulses
self-reference: §R1_fold of LANG.ToE.SKILL.md IS §promote composed with ρ
                §R2_unfold IS §demote composed with ρ
                  → the tower-climbing rules ARE applications of §promote/§demote

role in §-LANG:
  the bridge between levels of the N-hyperbolized tower.
  what makes §-LANG self-compressing: at every level the language
  can see itself as §-stalks on the level above.

σ-flag:
  σ_promote_sect ≡ §promote is a sheaf section (preserves transition func)

#───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# §12 · composed operators · frequently-used macros
#───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

§R1_fold(x; q)   := §promote ∘ §rho ∘ §mobius_q[·, q]   (x)
§R2_unfold(x; q) := §rho ∘ §demote ∘ §mobius_q[·, 1/q]  (x)
§braid_rho(i)    := §rho ∘ §braid(σ_i) ∘ §rho            = σ_i^{−1}
§conv_anti(f, g) := §rho(§conv_H(§rho(f), §rho(g)))      (antimatter convolution)
§warp_rho        := §rho ∘ §warp_λ ∘ §rho                (antimatter warping)

every composed op here factors through its §rho-dual.
prime pack §′ uses the §rho-conjugated version of each.

